import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'wrong-return':('Two adjacent monsters, the dangerous one examined first','A level-30 Blackguard stands between an adjacent master lich (examined first, scoring 234 with the danger bonus) and an adjacent kobold (examined second, scoring 30). The chooser\'s real call re-runs the attack to execute it and reports the value; the original returns the last monster\'s 30, the correction returns the best one\'s 234.'),
 'single':('Control: only the lich','With one monster the last examined and the best are the same. The complete logs are byte-identical.'),
 'none':('Control: nothing adjacent','With no monsters both versions return nothing. The complete logs are byte-identical.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text()
  entry={'raw':raw,'passed':'native-c/maimfoe-256 finished: 1/1 passed' in raw}
  for tag,key in (('SETUP blows=','setup'),('REALCALL ','realcall'),('OUTCOME ','outcome')):
   match=re.search(re.escape(tag)+r'(.*)',raw)
   entry[key]={k:int(v) for k,v in re.findall(r'(\w+)=(-?\d+)',match[1])} if match else None
  item[phase]=entry
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Maim Foe reported the last monster it looked at</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.num{font-size:34px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:30px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native Maim Foe scores</p><h1>Maim Foe reported the last monster it looked at</h1><p>The Maim Foe attack scan tracks the best adjacent target and its score. The simulation pass reports that best score, but the real execution pass — the one that actually aims and casts — returned the loop variable holding the last monster it happened to examine. With two adjacent monsters where the dangerous one is examined first, the cast went to the right target while the reported score belonged to the trivial one. The correction returns the tracked best score.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><br><button data-step="0">The targets</button><button data-step="1">The reported score</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2>Corrected</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the controls establish</h2><p>With only the lich, last and best are the same monster and both versions report the same score; with nothing adjacent, both report nothing. Those complete logs match byte for byte, so the correction changes only the two-monster case.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Blackguard level 30, depth 30, seed 1000, glowing constructed arena, the Fear and Torment book carried, Maim Foe learned (two blows at this level). The chooser's real-path entry point is called directly with the target list the attack chooser would have filled (recorded as a fixture intervention); the cast keys are queued, not executed. The chooser currently discards this real-path value, so the measured wrongness is in the reported score itself, not in a different cast today.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Corrected</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/256">issue256</a>.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;let step=1;const select=document.getElementById('scenario');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}
function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared','after']]){let d=c[phase],p=document.getElementById(panel);p.querySelector('.num').textContent=step===0?`Targets: ${c.label.startsWith('Control: nothing')?'none':(c.label.startsWith('Control: only')?'the lich':'lich then kobold')}.`:`Reported score: ${d.realcall?d.realcall.value:'?'}.`;p.querySelector('.state').textContent=step===0?'Both are adjacent; the lich scores far higher.':'The real execution pass reports its score.';p.querySelector('.action').textContent=step===1?(d.realcall&&d.realcall.value>100?'Reports the lich\\'s score.':'Reports the kobold\\'s score.'):'';document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}
document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='wrong-return'?'The original reports the kobold\\'s 30; the correction reports the lich\\'s 234.':'Both versions agree in this control; the logs match byte for byte.';for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.classList.toggle('active',Number(b.dataset.step)===step)}
select.addEventListener('change',()=>{step=1;draw()});for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{step=Number(b.dataset.step);draw()});draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
